.TH "SLIPWAY-GET" "1" "2026-09-30" "slipway 0.1.0" "Slipway Manual"
.SH NAME
slipway\-get \- Display one or many resources
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY "slipway get"
.I "(TYPE [NAME...] | TYPE/NAME...)"\&
.RI [ flags ]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
Display one or many resources.
.PP
Prints a table of the most important information about the specified resources. You can filter the list using a label selector and the \-\-selector flag, or a field selector and the \-\-field\-selector flag. Projects are listed in the current group unless you pass \-\-all\-groups.
.PP
Use \-o wide to add the path, the head commit, the age of the last commit and the drift of each project: the ways its repository differs from its manifest and what keeps sync from converging it. Use \-o json or \-o yaml for the full object with its status.
.PP
Resource types: projects (project, proj) and groups (group). Type words are case\-insensitive.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIFORMAT\fR
Output format. One of: table, wide, json, yaml, name. (default "table")
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-selector\fR \fIEXPR\fR
Selector (label query) to filter on, supports '=', '==', '!=', 'in', 'notin' (e.g. \-l key1=value1,key2=value2,key3 in (value3)). Matching objects must satisfy all of the specified label constraints.
.TP
\fB\-\-field\-selector\fR \fIEXPR\fR
Selector (field query) to filter on, supports '=', '==', and '!=' (e.g. \-\-field\-selector key1=value1,key2=value2). Projects support metadata.name, metadata.group, spec.path, status.state, status.branch, status.lastFetch; groups support metadata.name. Values compare exactly, case included, with the object \-o json prints: spec.path as registered, status.lastFetch as an RFC 3339 time. A field the object leaves out compares as the empty value, except status.lastFetch, which compares as never. A backslash escapes a backslash, a comma or an equals sign in a value.
.TP
\fB\-A\fR, \fB\-\-all\-groups\fR
If present, list the requested object(s) across all groups. The group in the current configuration is ignored even if specified with \-\-group.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
When using the default output format, don't print headers.
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-labels\fR
When printing, show all labels as the last column.
.SH COLUMNS
Projects show NAME, BRANCH, STATUS, FETCHED and AGE; \-\-all\-groups adds GROUP in front, \-o wide adds PATH, HEAD, LAST\-COMMIT and DRIFT, and \-\-show\-labels adds LABELS. Groups show NAME, PROJECTS and AGE, and \-o wide adds DESCRIPTION. A cell slipway has no value for reads <none>, as every cell from git does when git cannot read the repository.
.TP
\fBGROUP\fR
The group of the project.
.TP
\fBNAME\fR
The name of the resource.
.TP
\fBBRANCH\fR
The checked\-out branch, or (detached) when HEAD points at a commit.
.TP
\fBSTATUS\fR
One word for the state of the repository, from the list below.
.TP
\fBFETCHED\fR
Time since the repository was last fetched, by slipway or by git itself and from any of its worktrees. <never> means git answered and no fetch is on record, which includes a last fetch that failed.
.TP
\fBAGE\fR
Time since the resource was registered, in kubectl's units (3s, 4m12s, 11h, 2y319d).
.TP
\fBPATH\fR
The registered path, as the manifest writes it.
.TP
\fBHEAD\fR
The abbreviated id of the checked\-out commit.
.TP
\fBLAST\-COMMIT\fR
The age of the checked\-out commit.
.TP
\fBDRIFT\fR
The ways the repository differs from its manifest and the blocker that keeps sync from fast\-forwarding it, as slipway diff names them.
.TP
\fBPROJECTS\fR
The number of projects in the group.
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
The description of the group.
.TP
\fBLABELS\fR
The labels, as key=value pairs.
.SH "STATUS WORDS"
STATUS is the first of these words that holds, in this order.
.TP
\fBMissing\fR
The registered path is relative, or is not a directory on this machine.
.TP
\fBNotARepo\fR
The directory exists but no repository contains it.
.TP
\fBUnsafe\fR
git refused the repository because another user owns it (safe.directory); describe, diff and fetch print the git command that trusts it.
.TP
\fBConflicted\fR
The working tree has unmerged paths.
.TP
\fBDetached\fR
HEAD points at a commit rather than a branch.
.TP
\fBUnborn\fR
The branch has no commits yet.
.TP
\fBDirty\fR
Staged, modified or untracked files are present.
.TP
\fBGone\fR
An upstream is configured but its remote\-tracking ref is gone, as of the last fetch \-\-prune (or a fetch with fetch.prune set).
.TP
\fBDiverged\fR
The branch is both ahead of and behind its upstream, as of the last fetch (FETCHED).
.TP
\fBAhead\fR
Commits not yet pushed to the upstream, as of the last fetch (FETCHED).
.TP
\fBBehind\fR
Commits on the upstream not yet pulled, as of the last fetch (FETCHED).
.TP
\fBClean\fR
Nothing to do.
.TP
\fBUnknown\fR
git could not answer: it is not installed, it did not finish within 10 seconds, or it failed for a reason slipway does not classify. Each distinct reason is printed once on stderr per run.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
# List all projects in the current group
slipway get projects
.EE
.PP
.EX
# List all projects in every group, with the path and last commit
slipway get projects \-A \-o wide
.EE
.PP
.EX
# List a single project in YAML output format
slipway get project hldr \-o yaml
.EE
.PP
.EX
# List the projects labeled lang=rust
slipway get projects \-l lang=rust
.EE
.PP
.EX
# List the projects in every group that are not clean
slipway get projects \-A \-\-field\-selector status.state!=Clean
.EE
.PP
.EX
# List the projects no fetch has reached
slipway get projects \-\-field\-selector status.lastFetch=never
.EE
.PP
.EX
# List every group
slipway get groups
.EE
